sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant RHODS as rhods-operator
    participant User as Component / User
    participant API as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Op as db-operator<br/>odh-db-operator-operator
    participant CM as cert-manager
    participant PG as PostgreSQL provider<br/>Internal 5432/TCP or External
    participant WL as Consuming workload
    participant Prom as Prometheus /<br/>data-science-collector

    Note over RHODS,PG: Flow 1 - Module enablement and default provider
    RHODS->>API: Create DatabaseService/default-db-operator, install chart<br/>TLS 1.2+, SA token
    API-->>Op: Watch event (DatabaseService)
    Op->>API: Apply infrastructure CRDs, create DatabaseProvider rhai-db<br/>TLS 1.2+, SA token
    Op->>API: Render StatefulSet, Service, PVC, admin Secret,<br/>NetworkPolicy, Issuer/Certificate, SCC RoleBinding
    CM->>API: Issue Internal TLS Secret
    Op->>PG: Reachability / version check<br/>5432/TCP, TLS verify-full, postgres admin password
    PG-->>Op: Server version, TLS state
    Op->>API: Update DatabaseProvider / DatabaseService status

    Note over User,WL: Flow 2 - Claim provisioning and consumption
    User->>API: Create DatabaseClaim / SchemaClaim<br/>TLS 1.2+, user/SA token + RBAC
    API-->>Op: Watch event (claim)
    Op->>Op: Select provider (name / label, selection-priority, ties by name)
    Op->>PG: CREATE DATABASE/SCHEMA, ROLE, GRANT, extensions<br/>TLS verify-full (Internal) / require (External), admin creds
    PG-->>Op: OK
    Op->>API: Write connection Secret in claim namespace<br/>host, port, user, password, dbname, sslmode[, schema, ca.crt]
    Op->>API: Update Internal NetworkPolicy allow-list (claim namespace)
    WL->>API: Mount connection Secret
    WL->>PG: Connect 5432/TCP<br/>per Secret sslmode (+ca.crt), per-claim role/password

    Note over Prom,Op: Flow 3 - Metrics scraping
    Prom->>Op: GET /metrics 8443/TCP HTTPS<br/>TLS service-ca, Bearer token
    Op->>API: TokenReview + SubjectAccessReview
    API-->>Op: Allowed (get /metrics)
    Op-->>Prom: Prometheus metrics
